### 4.5 Core API sketch

```crystal
# src/llm/protocol_kind.cr
module LLM
  enum ProtocolKind
    ChatCompletions
    Responses
  end
end

# src/llm/function_call.cr
module LLM
  # Canonical "the model asked to call this tool". Stable JSON shape:
  # {"id": ..., "name": ..., "arguments": "<json string>"}
  class FunctionCall
    include JSON::Serializable

    getter id : String
    getter name : String
    getter arguments : String

    def initialize(@id, @name, @arguments = "")
    end
  end
end
```

`LLM::Chat` keeps its existing config surface (`with_model`, `with_system_message`,
`with_streaming`, `with_readonly`, `with_tool`, …) and gains everything that was
moved up out of `OpenAI::Chat`:

```crystal
# src/llm/chat.cr (sketch — existing config/tool registry omitted)
module LLM
  abstract class Chat
    private getter history : History
    getter usage : Usage?

    # -- Session management: moved up from OpenAI::Chat, logic unchanged --
    # erase_history / save / load / fork / squish / tail / send_tail /
    # append_conversations / extract_conversations /
    # append_last_response_as_prompt / import / append_message

    # -- Query loop --
    def ask(content : String, attach : ChatInclusions? = nil,
            response_schema : ResponseSchema? = nil,
            exclude_reasoning_in_history : Bool = false,
            exclude_reasoning_skip : Int32 = 0, & : ChatEvent ->)
      append_message Message::MultiContent.new(prompt: content, attach: attach)
      post_session(response_schema, exclude_reasoning_in_history, exclude_reasoning_skip) do |ev|
        yield ev
      end
    end

    def re_ask(response_schema : ResponseSchema? = nil,
               exclude_reasoning_in_history : Bool = false,
               exclude_reasoning_skip : Int32 = 0, & : ChatEvent ->)
      post_session(response_schema, exclude_reasoning_in_history, exclude_reasoning_skip) do |ev|
        yield ev
      end
    end

    # -- Tool execution: moved up; boundary is now canonical FunctionCall --
    def call_tools_and_setup_ask(tool_calls : Array(FunctionCall), & : ChatEvent ->) : Int32
      # find_tool?(name) / tool.run(args) / append Message::ToolCall +
      # attachments / unknown-tool error message — same logic as today
    end

    # -- The ONE protocol contract --
    # Encode the current session, POST it, yield canonical events, and
    # append the resulting Message::Response (with Usage) to history.
    abstract def post_session(response_schema : ResponseSchema? = nil,
                              exclude_reasoning_in_history : Bool = false,
                              exclude_reasoning_skip : Int32 = 0,
                              & : ChatEvent ->) : Nil
  end
end
```

A protocol `Chat` therefore only implements `post_session` plus its
encode/decode helpers. `LLM::Connection#post_and_stream` gains an optional
per-call path argument (default `self.path`) so a Responses chat can hit
`/v1/responses` on the same client/connection:

```crystal
protected def post_and_stream(path : String? = nil, body, session_id : String? = nil, &)
```

### 4.6 Canonical event vocabulary

The app layer (`session.cr`) keeps consuming exactly these events; decoders
map protocol events onto them. `Events` constants (new `events.cr`) replace
the string literals.

| Event | Content (canonical) | ChatCompletions source | Responses source |
|---|---|---|---|
| `debug/request`, `debug/data` | raw JSON | as today | as today |
| `text` | String (delta while streaming, whole otherwise) | `choices[0].delta.content` | `response.output_text.delta` |
| `reasoning` | String | `reasoning` / `reasoning_content` / `thinking` | `response.reasoning_summary_text.delta` |
| `receiving_tool_call` | String (tool name) | first `tool_calls` chunk with a name | `response.output_item.added` with `function_call` |
| `tool_call_requested` | `FunctionCall` JSON `{id, name, arguments}` | completed `tool_calls` chunk (was `{id, function:{…}}` — **shape change**) | `response.function_call_arguments.done` |
| `calling_tool` | `FunctionCall` JSON | as today (**shape change**) | same as today's semantics |
| `tool_call/done` | `{id, name, output}` JSON | `ToolCall#emit` (key names normalized) | same |
| `finish_reason` | String | `choices[0].finish_reason` | `response.completed.status` |
| `usage` | `Usage` JSON (prompt/completion/total) | `usage` field, `prompt_tokens`… | `response.completed.usage`, `input_tokens`… |
| `done` | null | `[DONE]` | `response.completed` / stream end |
| `error/server` | raw error JSON | `data["error"]` | `response.failed` / `error` events |
| `error/unexpected` | headers/body | as today | as today |
| `error/unknown_tool_call` | `FunctionCall` JSON | as today (**shape change**) | same |

`tool_call_merge` (CC-internal chunk merging) becomes a private concern of the
CC decoder and is no longer part of the public vocabulary.

