## 6. Provider wiring

**Rule: every provider speaks exactly one protocol at a time — the
highest-fidelity protocol its backend supports.** Responses is that protocol
where the backend is real OpenAI. ChatCompletions survives only as a
compatibility path: CC-only backends, legacy deployments, or an explicit
override for legacy behavior.

```crystal
# src/llm/openai/connection.cr (sketch)
module LLM::OpenAI
  class Connection < LLM::Connection
    # The highest-fidelity protocol this backend speaks.
    # Ollama / GoogleAIStudio connections declare ChatCompletions.
    def protocol : LLM::ProtocolKind
      LLM::ProtocolKind::Responses
    end

    # `nil` -> the provider's declared protocol.
    def new_chat(protocol : LLM::ProtocolKind? = nil, &) : LLM::Chat
      p = protocol || self.protocol
      case p
      when .responses?        then Protocol::Responses::Chat.new(self, &.)
      when .chat_completions? then Protocol::ChatCompletions::Chat.new(self, &.)
      end
    end

    def protocol_path(kind : LLM::ProtocolKind) : String
      case kind
      when .chat_completions? then "/v1/chat/completions"
      when .responses?        then "/v1/responses"
      end
    end
  end
end
```

`LLM::Connection` (base) gains `abstract def protocol : LLM::ProtocolKind` so
the app can uniformly query what a provider speaks and validate overrides.

Protocol per provider (v1):

| Provider | Declared (primary) protocol | ChatCompletions |
|---|---|---|
| OpenAI | Responses | compatibility override — e.g. self-hosted OpenAI-compatible servers (via `OPENAI_ENDPOINT`) that only implement CC |
| Azure OpenAI | Responses (verify the deployment's api-version supports it) | compatibility override — legacy deployments |
| Azure Foundry | Responses (verify) | compatibility override |
| Ollama | ChatCompletions | — (only protocol it speaks) |
| Google AI Studio | ChatCompletions | — (only protocol it speaks) |

**Deliberate behavior change:** new OpenAI/Azure sessions default to the
Responses protocol; prior behavior remains available via the CC override.

Selection: optional `protocol` field on the LLM/model config entry (default:
the provider's declared protocol); `Session#setup_chat` passes it to
`new_chat`. A provider + protocol combination the backend can't serve raises
a clear error at session start.

