## 7. Migration plan

No unit specs exist for this module today, so every phase must be verified by
`crystal build` + a manual smoke matrix: *plain ask (streaming + non),
tool-call round-trip, session save → restore → continue, fork*. Capture
golden files (request bodies, recorded SSE streams) **before** Phase 1 so
each phase has a regression baseline.

**Phase 0 — pure moves (no behavior change).**
Create `protocol/chat_completions/`; move files per §4.7; rename namespaces
(`LLM::OpenAI::Chat` → `LLM::Protocol::ChatCompletions::Chat`,
`LLM::OpenAI::History` → `LLM::History`, etc.); update requires in
`src/llm.cr`. `to_protocol_json` and all JSON shapes stay identical.
*Accept: smoke matrix passes; restored old session continues normally.*

**Phase 1 — canonical boundary types.**
Add `LLM::FunctionCall`, `LLM::Events`, `LLM::ProtocolKind`. Change
`call_tools_and_setup_ask` to `Array(FunctionCall)`; normalize
`tool_call_requested` / `calling_tool` / `error/unknown_tool_call` /
`tool_call/done` event content to the shapes in §4.6. Update the app side:
`session.cr` (`tools` array type, `process_event` digs,
`renderer.llm_tool_call` args) and the recorder (event payloads change;
recorder is a debug artifact — document the drift).
*Accept: smoke matrix; recorded sessions still load.*

**Phase 2 — lift shared logic into `LLM::Chat`.**
Move session management + tool loop + `ask`/`re_ask` up per §4.5; define
abstract `post_session`; slim the CC `Chat` to encode/decode only; delete
`to_protocol_json`/`protocol_fields_to_json` from canonical `Message` (the
CC encoder encodes directly); align `re_ask` signatures (add
`exclude_reasoning_skip` to the abstract).
*Accept: smoke matrix; `to_json` (save) output byte-identical to pre-refactor.*

**Phase 3 — Responses adapter.**
Implement `LLM::Protocol::Responses::{Chat, Encoder, Decoder,
FunctionCallBuilder}`; wire the provider protocol declaration (`protocol` +
`new_chat` + `protocol_path`) and the CC compatibility override (config
field); golden-file tests for encoder (canned session: system,
user + attachments, assistant + tool round-trip) and decoder (recorded real
SSE stream).
*Accept: a full tool-calling conversation against the live Responses API
(same prompts as the smoke matrix); save/restore round-trip.*

**Phase 4 — hardening (optional).**
Add a `specs/` directory with unit specs over the golden fixtures; per-call
path override on `Connection#post_and_stream` if the Azure deployment quirk
demands it; investigate `previous_response_id` chaining as a token-saving
mode; consider Responses built-in tools.

